NNOOTTEESS
       While  one  thread is blocked in a call to eeppoollll__wwaaiitt(), it is possible
       for another thread to add a file descriptor to  the  waited‐upon  eeppoollll
       instance.   If the new file descriptor becomes ready, it will cause the
       eeppoollll__wwaaiitt() call to unblock.

       If more than _n file descriptors are ready when eeppoollll__wwaaiitt() is  called,
       then  successive eeppoollll__wwaaiitt() calls will round robin through the set of
       ready file descriptors.  This behavior helps avoid  starvation  scenar‐
       ios,  where  a process fails to notice that additional file descriptors
       are ready because it focuses on a set of file descriptors that are  al‐
       ready known to be ready.

       Note  that  it  is  possible  to call eeppoollll__wwaaiitt() on an eeppoollll instance
       whose interest list is currently empty (or whose interest list  becomes
       empty  because file descriptors are closed or removed from the interest
       in another thread).  The call will block until some file descriptor  is
       later  added to the interest list (in another thread) and that file de‐
       scriptor becomes ready.

